WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.635
In 1644, the Ming dynasty came to its end.

00:00:03.635 --> 00:00:07.655
General Wu Sangui was guarding the important Shanhai Pass.

00:00:07.655 --> 00:00:11.831
In the distance, Shanhai Pass firmly guarded the gateway to the north.

00:00:11.831 --> 00:00:15.673
Li Zicheng's great army fought its way all the way into Beijing.

00:00:15.673 --> 00:00:19.041
Wu Sangui was very anxious and decided to ask the Qing army for help.

00:00:19.041 --> 00:00:23.632
He wrote the letter asking for help and sent it out overnight by fast horse.

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:27.050
The regent Dorgon led the Qing army to the front of the pass.

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:31.342
The city gates opened, and the two armies joined forces to face Li Zicheng in battle.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:35.013
Li Zicheng's army was badly defeated and had no choice but to withdraw from Beijing.

00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:38.592
Dorgon led the Qing army and entered Beijing smoothly.

00:00:38.592 --> 00:00:42.124
The Qing army was strictly disciplined, and the city gradually grew calm.

00:00:42.124 --> 00:00:45.404
A few months later, the young Emperor Shunzhi arrived in Beijing.

00:00:45.404 --> 00:00:48.963
He was only six years old, sitting in the carriage and looking around curiously.

00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:52.359
Common people stood by the streets, whispering and talking among themselves.

00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:55.721
From this year on, the Qing dynasty began to rule the Central Plains.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.467
From then on, Chinese history turned to a new page.
